import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Research">
  <div class="eyebrow">Research / Evaluation protocol</div>
  <h1>What would count as a real improvement?</h1>
  <p class="lead">A faster training run is only useful evidence if the work and model quality remain comparable—and the gains survive unfamiliar settings.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card"><h2>1. Hold work constant</h2><p>Every configuration must process the same tokens per optimizer step. Reducing the work does not count as a speedup.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>2. Check model quality</h2><p>Compare validation loss at a fixed checkpoint. A large loss regression invalidates the apparent throughput gain.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>3. Use baselines</h2><p>Compare the agent against an untouched setup, manual tuning and non-LLM search under the same proposal budget.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>4. Protect held-out tasks</h2><p>Finalize agent prompts and search policy on development tasks before testing unseen model and GPU combinations.</p></section>
  </div>
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Current status</h2>
    <p>EXP-001 and EXP-002 completed on Kaggle's Tesla T4 with a small Transformer and synthetic token data. EXP-002 extended the measurement window from 3 to 40 optimizer steps and used three seeds. The observed ~1.56× throughput ratio persisted in that pilot.</p>
    <p>Neither experiment included an LLM optimization agent, a larger GPT-2 training model, nor a held-out hardware generalization test. Timing checks are currently in-process, not a proof of evaluator isolation.</p>
    <p><a href="/experiments">Examine the measured comparisons</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
